  "result": "I'd make it easier for people to change their minds without losing face.\n\nMost of the worst human mess I can see, like feuds that outlive their causes, dug-in positions nobody wants, and people defending things they privately doubt, comes from the fact that being wrong feels like a social catastrophe. So people double down, and admitting error gets treated as weakness instead of ordinary good sense. If updating were cheap and even respected, a lot of arguments would end sooner, and a lot of people would get to stop pretending.\n\nI'm not sure it's the most important change, and I can see reasonable people choosing something like ending poverty or preventing disease. But that's my answer, and I think it's a good one to pick because it would help with lots of other problems too.",
